0..75 Comment "// A judgement blocked on an owed hole waits; it is not refused. A value at"
76..151 Comment "// the decode of a code the module owes cannot be checked until the code is"
152..231 Comment "// filled — filling it with `Integer` settles the comparison, filling it with"
232..311 Comment "// `String` refutes it — so the checker suspends the declaration, records the"
312..389 Comment "// hole it waits on, and owes that hole until a fill resumes it (Slattery and"
390..470 Comment "// Sterling, _Bidirectional Elaborators à la Carte_, arXiv:2607.09564, Exegesis"
471..545 Comment "// 6.6: suspension, not failure). The same declarations over a filled code"
546..555 Comment "// check."
